摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Goal-driven multi-agent orchestration for DeepSeek Harness — bounded DAG scheduling, nested delegation, typed evidence, and durable trajectory UI.","id":"gh:1343875138","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-goalmesh","slug":"Jarad-z/dsh-goalmesh","topics":["agent-orchestration","agentic-workflow","cordis","dag-scheduler","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","goal-driven","multi-agent","multi-agent-systems","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Goal-driven multi-agent orchestration for DeepSeek Harness — bounded DAG scheduling, nested delegati"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"on, typed evidence, and durable trajectory UI."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"English"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Goal-driven multi-agent orchestration for DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Turn one objective into a bounded agent graph—and keep every decision, dependency, and result observ"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"one objective into a bounded agent graph—and keep every decision, dependency, and result observable."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Why ·\nHow it works ·\nCapabilities ·\nProtocol ·\nDevelopment"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## One goal in. A coordinated mesh out."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"DSH GoalMesh is a DeepSeek Harness\nPlugin that exposes one model-facing tool: **`goal_mesh`**. It va"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"lidates a declarative\ntask DAG, launches bounded specialist agents, propagates typed dependency resu"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"lts,\nsupports nested decomposition, and renders the full execution trajectory in DSH Web."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"01 · Goal-native\nEvery agent receives the immutable global goal, a focused objective, and explicit a"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ery agent receives the immutable global goal, a focused objective, and explicit acceptance criteria."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"02 · Multi-agent by design\nDAG scheduling, bounded concurrency, nested delegation, deadlines, and ca"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ncellation share one owner."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"03 · Evidence-first\nTyped reports and durable events make live execution and replay explainable from"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" the same task tree."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> GoalMesh is a **DSH Plugin**, not a Codex Plugin. It runs inside the DeepSeek\n> Harness "},{"id":"p12s2","text":"Profile and follows Cordis Entry/Fiber lifecycle ownership."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Why GoalMesh"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- **Goal fidelity** — local work remains anchored to the same success criteria and constraints.\n- **"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"Structured concurrency** — admission, deadlines, cancellation, failure propagation, and cleanup are "},{"id":"p14s3","text":"bounded by one coordinator.\n- **Dependency-aware execution** — tasks start only after prerequisites "},{"id":"p14s4","text":"settle, with explicit `fail`, `skip`, or `partial` behavior.\n- **Safe recursive delegation** — child"},{"id":"p14s5","text":" agents can open nested meshes through attempt-fenced, child-scoped leases.\n- **Stable typed results"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"** — every child returns a `TaskReport`; task identity and input order remain deterministic.\n- **Dur"},{"id":"p14s7","text":"able observability** — live events and replay fold into the same Web task tree, including trusted ch"},{"id":"p14s8","text":"ild-Session navigation."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The coordinator sits above root and child agents. Children never receive the mutable\nrun ledger; the"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"y operate through revocable leases, so siblings cannot mutate one\nanother's state. Cordis fibers own"},{"id":"p17s3","text":" every tool registration, listener, service, and live\nresource from mount through disposal."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Capabilities"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| Capability | v0.3 |\n|---|:---:|\n| Foreground bounded parallelism | ✅ |\n| Static task DAGs and depe"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"ndency materialization | ✅ |\n| Collect-all, fail-fast, and quorum policies | ✅ |\n| Fail, skip, and p"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"artial dependency propagation | ✅ |\n| Nested local GoalMesh calls | ✅ |\n| Parent permit release/reac"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"quire during nested work | ✅ |\n| Durable trajectory replay and Web task tree | ✅ |\n| Runtime invaria"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"nt validation | ✅ |\n| Detached/background execution | Planned |\n| Automatic task retry | Planned |\n|"},{"id":"p19s6","text":" Distributed provider-aware capacity | Planned |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Package layout"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"| Package | Responsibility |"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"| `dsh-goalmesh-plugin` | Installable composition bundle and Cordis patch |\n| `dsh-tool-goalmesh` | "},{"id":"p22s2","text":"Host tool, coordinator, scheduler, recorder, and invariant companion |\n| `dsh-client-ui-goalmesh` | "},{"id":"p22s3","text":"Inert Node entry and DSH Web trajectory client |"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"The split follows DeepSeek Harness ownership boundaries: Host scheduling works in a\nheadless Profile"},{"id":"p24s2","text":", while the installable bundle composes Host, invariant, and Web entries."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Tool protocol"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"A root invocation declares one goal and an invocation-local task graph:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Nested invocations omit `goal`. Ownership comes from the scoped lease captured by the\nHost tool—neve"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"r from model-provided IDs."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"GoalMesh v0.3 targets DeepSeek Harness `0.1.0-rc.5` at public baseline\n`47f943859bef60e4160492346772"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"ded9b24f765a`, plus the minimal runtime patch in\n`harness-patches/goalmesh-prerequisites.patch`."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Keep `deepseek-harness` and `dsh-goalmesh` as sibling directories. Workspace\n> depe"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"ndencies intentionally resolve against that layout."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"### Useful commands"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"| Command | Purpose |"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| `pnpm build` | Build Host and Web packages |\n| `pnpm typecheck` | Check the full TypeScript projec"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"t graph |\n| `pnpm test:unit` | Run the Vitest suite |\n| `pnpm lint` | Run oxlint |\n| `pnpm check` | "},{"id":"p35s3","text":"Build, test, and lint—the CI contract |"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"Build artifacts are emitted under `packages/tool-goalmesh/lib/` and\n`packages/client-ui-goalmesh/lib"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"/`. The ready-to-compose Profile patch lives at\n`packages/goalmesh-plugin/cordis.patch.yml`."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## Design guarantees"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"- The root tool returns only after its invocation and owned resources settle.\n- Unknown model fields"},{"id":"p38s2","text":" and forged ownership identifiers are rejected.\n- The global goal is read-only; children report only"},{"id":"p38s3","text":" against local task goals.\n- Coordinator transitions are serialized and checked by runtime invariant"},{"id":"p38s4","text":"s.\n- Durable UI events are observational; the Web client never becomes a second scheduler.\n- Provide"},{"id":"p38s5","text":"r removal stops new admission without abandoning already-owned cleanup."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"Read the architecture contract for the complete design. Version\nboundaries and implementation order "},{"id":"p39s2","text":"are recorded in the execution plan."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"## Contributing"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"Contributions are welcome. Start with CONTRIBUTING.md and run\n`pnpm check` before opening a pull req"},{"id":"p41s2","text":"uest. Report security issues through GitHub's\nprivate vulnerability reporting flow described in SECU"},{"id":"p41s3","text":"port security issues through GitHub's\nprivate vulnerability reporting flow described in SECURITY.md."},{"id":"p42s1","text":"Released under the MIT License."},{"id":"p43s1","text":"Built for explicit goals, bounded agents, and inspectable outcomes."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
